{% comment %}
  ============================================================================
  Learn Page — combined, filterable Article feed (task 0007, round 2)
  ============================================================================
  Production (LearnPage.tsx) shows one flat, client-side-filterable article grid with category
  buttons (All / Soil Education / Sustainability / ...) plus a single always-visible featured
  article above it. DXB's articles live across SEPARATE Shopify Blogs by category (Soil
  Science / Soil Education / Sustainability, confirmed via Admin's blog-posts list), not tags
  within one blog — so this section merges up to 4 blogs into one feed with a real client-side
  filter, matching production's exact UX rather than falling back to stacked single-blog
  sections.

  WHY FIXED CATEGORY SETTINGS, NOT A BLOCK REPEATER: a block-repeater (one block per category,
  each with its own blog picker) looks like the natural fit, but this project already hit a hard
  wall on this exact pattern — see .claude/CLAUDE.md's "Theme Blocks Must Render Themselves":
  external blocks/*.liquid files can't have their settings read from outside their own render
  (block.type reports as the literal string "@theme" at runtime, block.settings.* from the
  parent's context comes back blank). Merging multiple blogs' articles into one combined,
  filterable list requires this section to read each category's blog picker directly at render
  time — impossible with real theme blocks. Fixed section-level settings
  (category_1_blog/category_1_label ... category_4_blog/category_4_label) are the only
  architecturally valid way to do this. 4 slots covers the 3 known categories with one spare;
  any slot left with no blog picked is skipped entirely, no error.

  FEATURED ARTICLE: Shopify Articles have no native "featured" boolean. Uses a tag instead
  (default tag name "featured", configurable) — DXB adds that tag to one article in Admin to
  promote it; if no article across the configured blogs carries the tag, the very first article
  found is used instead so the section never renders with an empty featured slot. The featured
  article always shows regardless of which category filter is active, matching production (only
  the grid below responds to the filter buttons).

  READ TIME: not a native Article field either. Estimated from word count
  (`content | strip_html | split: ' ' | size`, ~200 words/minute, floored at 1) — an approximation,
  not pulled from any real per-article field, since none exists to pull from.

  FILTER INTERACTION: vanilla JS, no dependencies — toggles a `hidden` attribute on cards whose
  `data-category` doesn't match the clicked filter button (`data-filter="all"` shows everything).
  Progressive enhancement: with JS disabled, every card stays visible (default, no `hidden`
  attribute set server-side), so nothing breaks, it just isn't filterable.

  COLOR: no hardcoded hex. Accent resolves through `section.settings.accent_color`, falling back
  to `color_palette.color3`. Section background falls back to `color_palette.color11` (light,
  matching production's light page background) via `section.settings.background_color`.

  DEPLOY: written directly into this live repo's working tree as part of the 2026-09-07
  live-edit pilot (see claude_docs/build_docs/live_edit_pilot_plan.md) — DXB reviews, then
  commits and pushes by hand.
  ============================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  assign accent = section.settings.accent_color | default: settings.color_palette.color3
  assign bg = section.settings.background_color | default: settings.color_palette.color11
  assign featured_tag = section.settings.featured_tag | default: 'featured'

  if section.settings.background_color != blank
    render 'contrast-override', background_color: section.settings.background_color, section_id: section.id, skip_contrast: true
  endif
%}

<div
  id="LearnArticles-{{ section.id }}"
  class="bfbella-learn-articles{% if section.settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}"
  style="
    --bfbella-accent: {{ accent }};
    --bfbella-bg: {{ bg }};
    {% if section.settings.padding_top != blank %}--bfbella-pad-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;{% endif %}
    {% if section.settings.padding_bottom != blank %}--bfbella-pad-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;{% endif %}
  "
>
  <div class="bfbella-learn-articles__inner page-width">
    {%- liquid
      assign featured_article = blank
      assign filter_buttons = ''
      assign cards_html = ''
      assign category_count = 0

      for i in (1..4)
        case i
          when 1
            assign cat_blog = section.settings.category_1_blog
            assign cat_label = section.settings.category_1_label
          when 2
            assign cat_blog = section.settings.category_2_blog
            assign cat_label = section.settings.category_2_label
          when 3
            assign cat_blog = section.settings.category_3_blog
            assign cat_label = section.settings.category_3_label
          when 4
            assign cat_blog = section.settings.category_4_blog
            assign cat_label = section.settings.category_4_label
        endcase

        if cat_blog != blank and cat_label != blank
          assign category_count = category_count | plus: 1
          assign cat_key = cat_label | handleize
          assign filter_buttons = filter_buttons | append: '<button type="button" class="bfbella-learn-articles__filter" data-filter="' | append: cat_key | append: '">' | append: cat_label | append: '</button>'

          for article in cat_blog.articles
            if featured_article == blank and article.tags contains featured_tag
              assign featured_article = article
              assign featured_category = cat_label
            endif

            assign word_count = article.content | strip_html | split: ' ' | size
            assign read_minutes = word_count | divided_by: 200
            assign read_minutes = read_minutes | at_least: 1
            assign excerpt = article.excerpt | default: article.content | strip_html | truncatewords: 22

            capture card
              render 'bfbella-learn-article-card', article: article, category_label: cat_label, category_key: cat_key, read_minutes: read_minutes, excerpt: excerpt
            endcapture
            assign cards_html = cards_html | append: card

            if featured_article == blank and forloop.index == 1 and i == 1
              assign fallback_article = article
              assign fallback_category = cat_label
            endif
          endfor
        endif
      endfor

      if featured_article == blank
        assign featured_article = fallback_article
        assign featured_category = fallback_category
      endif
    -%}

    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h1 class="bfbella-learn-articles__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
      <p class="bfbella-learn-articles__intro">{{ section.settings.intro }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if featured_article != blank -%}
      <a href="{{ featured_article.url }}" class="bfbella-learn-articles__featured">
        {%- if featured_article.image -%}
          <div class="bfbella-learn-articles__featured-media">
            <img
              src="{{ featured_article.image | image_url: width: 900 }}"
              alt="{{ featured_article.image.alt | escape }}"
              loading="lazy"
              width="900"
              height="{{ 900 | divided_by: featured_article.image.aspect_ratio }}"
            >
            <span class="bfbella-learn-articles__featured-badge">Featured Article</span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <div class="bfbella-learn-articles__featured-content">
          <div class="bfbella-learn-articles__featured-meta">
            <span class="bfbella-learn-articles__category">{{ featured_category }}</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="bfbella-learn-articles__featured-title">{{ featured_article.title }}</h2>
          {%- assign featured_excerpt = featured_article.excerpt | default: featured_article.content | strip_html | truncatewords: 30 -%}
          <p class="bfbella-learn-articles__featured-excerpt">{{ featured_excerpt }}</p>
          <span class="bfbella-learn-articles__featured-author">By {{ featured_article.author }}</span>
        </div>
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if category_count > 0 -%}
      <div class="bfbella-learn-articles__filters">
        <button type="button" class="bfbella-learn-articles__filter is-active" data-filter="all">{{ section.settings.all_label | default: 'All' }}</button>
        {{ filter_buttons }}
      </div>

      <div class="bfbella-learn-articles__grid">
        {{ cards_html }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .bfbella-learn-articles {
    position: relative;
    padding-block-start: var(--bfbella-pad-top, 3rem);
    padding-block-end: var(--bfbella-pad-bottom, 5rem);
    background-color: var(--bfbella-bg);
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__inner {
    max-width: 80rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: 1.5rem;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__heading {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-block-end: 1rem;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__intro {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    opacity: 0.75;
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-block-end: 2.5rem;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__featured {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    background-color: var(--color-background);
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.1);
    border-radius: 1.5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-block-end: 3rem;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 15px -3px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.08);
    transition: box-shadow 0.3s, border-color 0.3s;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__featured:hover {
    border-color: var(--bfbella-accent);
    box-shadow: 0 20px 25px -5px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1);
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__featured-media {
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    overflow: hidden;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      aspect-ratio: auto;
      height: 100%;
    }
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__featured-media img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    transition: transform 0.6s;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__featured:hover .bfbella-learn-articles__featured-media img {
    transform: scale(1.06);
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__featured-badge {
    position: absolute;
    top: 1.25rem;
    left: 1.25rem;
    background-color: var(--bfbella-accent);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__featured-content {
    padding: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      padding: 3rem;
    }
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__category {
    color: var(--bfbella-accent);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__featured-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-block: 0.75rem;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__featured-excerpt {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    opacity: 0.75;
    margin-block-end: 1rem;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__featured-author {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__filters {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-block-end: 2.5rem;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__filter {
    appearance: none;
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.15);
    background-color: var(--color-background);
    color: var(--color-foreground);
    padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: transform 0.2s, background-color 0.2s, color 0.2s;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__filter:hover {
    transform: scale(1.05);
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__filter.is-active {
    background-color: var(--bfbella-accent);
    border-color: var(--bfbella-accent);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;

    @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .bfbella-learn-articles__grid[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById('LearnArticles-{{ section.id }}');
    if (!root) return;
    var filters = root.querySelectorAll('.bfbella-learn-articles__filter');
    var cards = root.querySelectorAll('.bfbella-learn-article-card');
    filters.forEach(function (button) {
      button.addEventListener('click', function () {
        filters.forEach(function (b) { b.classList.remove('is-active'); });
        button.classList.add('is-active');
        var filter = button.getAttribute('data-filter');
        cards.forEach(function (card) {
          if (filter === 'all' || card.getAttribute('data-category') === filter) {
            card.hidden = false;
          } else {
            card.hidden = true;
          }
        });
      });
    });
  })();
</script>

